.TH NETSCOPE 1 "July 2026" "NetScope 0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
netscope \- reconnaissance and security analysis platform
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B netscope
[\fB\,-o\/\fR \fI\,format\/\fR] [\fB\,-v\/\fR] [\fB\,-q\/\fR] \fI\,command\/\fR [\fI\,args\/\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
NetScope discovers assets, analyzes services, identifies findings, and maps relationships in authorized environments.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIfmt\fR"
Output format: \fBtext\fR, \fBjson\fR, or \fBcsv\fR (default: text)
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress non-essential output
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help for a command
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B scan \fItarget\fR
Scan a target for assets and services. Optionally save results with \fB\-\-save\fR.
.TP
.B changes \fIpath\fR
Compare current state against the latest snapshot in the database.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Scan a target and display text output:
.B netcope scan 192.168.1.1
.TP
Scan and save to SQLite:
.B netcope scan example.com \-\-save assessment.db
.TP
Show changes since last snapshots:
.B netcope changes assessment.db
.TP
JSON output:
.B netcope scan 10.0.0.1 -o json
.SH FILES
.TP
.I assessment.db
SQLite database used with \fB\-\-save\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nmap (1),
.BR sqlite3 (1)
